==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|k|a}}

===Etymology===
An old Baltic loan; derived from the same word from which e.g. Lithuanian {{m|lt|gaũras}} is descended. Cognates include Veps and Estonian {{m|et|karv}} and Livonian {{m|liv|kōra}}. Originally ''karva'' only had the meaning "color". In its current meaning it is first mentioned in a biblical text in 1621.<ref>{{R:Hakkinen 2004}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈkɑrʋɑ]|lang=fi}}
* {{hyphenation|kar|va|lang=fi}}
* {{rhymes|ɑ|lang=fi}}

